TOTK: a mesh primitive's index vector stored whole by one thread where the host asks for it (the job's "mesh":
{"whole_indices": 1}, MeshStage.WholeIndices). The entry point let thread n store index byte n, so a triangle's three
components came from three threads. Without the field every translation is as before.

--- a/src/Ryujinx.Graphics.Shader/MeshStage.cs
+++ b/src/Ryujinx.Graphics.Shader/MeshStage.cs
@@ -43,6 +43,13 @@
         public int Debug { get; init; }
 
         /// <summary>
+        /// A primitive's index vector is stored whole, by the thread whose number is the primitive's. Otherwise thread n stores index
+        /// byte n, so the three components of a triangle's vector come from three threads, which a compiler that stores a component
+        /// by rewriting the vector loses.
+        /// </summary>
+        public bool WholeIndices { get; init; }
